{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, json, hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('runtime_view.json'));c=r['context'];history={h['id']:h for h in c['history']}\nheld_fixed=[\n 'Protocol 427fc51900560816321ba9bbc170639eb26625972df75b22e3c47d523c363748: released data identity, official split, four labels, official_offline visibility and 100-event maximum.',\n 'Same frozen scratch training: one epoch, batch8192, search seed20262027, split dense AdamW/embedding Adagrad, BF16, TF32 disabled, sum four BCEs, no loss hook.',\n 'Same static fields, global DIN bypass, 35 relation-by-quartile tokens, JointBlock, four task towers, eight feedback slots, bias-free 8D projection and zero-final-layer residual MLP.',\n 'Identical modules, parameter dimensions, RNG construction/reset order, initial tensors, raw feedback fractions/counts, user background and strength4; compute identity histogram and covariance in all arms.',\n 'Identical exposure-weighted content/fraction/covariance denominators, sanitization, task-mask intersection, zero target action, missing-ID treatment and empty-history residual masking.',\n 'Same validation macro-AUC selection/tie breakers; report four AUC/Logloss values, parameters, training/inference seconds, latency and memory.'\n]\nconfounds=[\n 'One search seed and repeated use of the same validation split; same-seed endpoint replay is calibration, not independent repeated support.',\n 'Changing either support changes optimization through the shared projection, residual MLP and eventually embedding parameters; a performance contrast does not prove independent statistical sampling.',\n 'Ad-ID concentration is an encoded-identity heuristic; OOV/nonpadding missing codes can collide. Historical task masks overlap and auxiliary positives are category/brand matches within24h, not ad-attributed conversions.',\n 'Ideal decomposition m*a_rate*(f-b)+a_cov*Cov(Wx,y) is approximate under inherited BF16 projection/rounding; preserve original operation order rather than algebraically refactoring.',\n 'Exposure and diversity controls share operation shapes, but measured runtime can vary; do not infer equal compute from equal parameter count.'\n]\ndef contrast(parent,intervention,control,supported,unsupported):\n return {'parent_ref':parent,'intervention':intervention,'control':control,'held_fixed':held_fixed,\n         'remaining_confounds':confounds,'decision_if_supported':supported,'decision_if_not_supported':unsupported}\nstudy={\n 'id':'g2-t001-component-specific-reliability',\n 'protocol_ref':r['required_study_protocol_ref'],\n 'evidence_refs':[\n 'baseline-din','g0-r0003-relation_content_counts','g2-r0004-count_shrink',\n 'g2-r0006-relation_count','g2-r0007-aligned_early_count','g2-r0007-aligned_late_count',\n 'g2-r0008-residual_count','g2-r0008-residual_fixed','g2-r0008-residual_marginal','g2-r0008-residual_content',\n 'g2-r0009-joint_count','g2-r0010-direct_count','g2-r0011-center_count',\n 'g2-r0012-context_cross_count','g2-r0012-context_add_count','g2-r0013-exclude_joint',\n 'g2-r0014-target_joint','g2-r0014-history_joint','g2-r0015-crossed_background','g2-r0015-user_background',\n 'g2-r0016-diversity_joint','g2-r0016-exposure_joint','g2-r0016-diversity_factorized','g2-r0016-exposure_factorized'],\n 'question':(\n 'Observation: round16 diversity support changes macro AUC by -0.000129235129 for joint moments but +0.000158080718 for factorized moments; the difference in differences is -0.000287315847 on one matched search seed. '\n 'Joint covariance changes AUC by -0.000135452548 under diversity versus +0.000151863300 under exposure. The incumbent g2-r0016-diversity_factorized scores0.828102187916, only0.000006217418 above exposure_joint0.828095970498, so its rank is preliminary. '\n 'Source inspection shows one support currently controls BOTH local-rate interpolation and covariance magnitude. Does separating these reliability assignments combine the diversity-rate advantage with the exposure-covariance advantage, exceeding both tied joint controls and the factorized incumbent at unchanged capacity and justified measured cost?'),\n 'hypothesis':(\n 'The marginal content-times-rate contrast and the within-slot event-feedback covariance can respond differently to duplicate-ad concentration. '\n 'For slot content mean m, fraction f, visible-user background b and covariance C, the centered joint feature is ideally a_rate*m*(f-b)+a_cov*C. '\n 'Current joint models force a_rate=a_cov=s/(s+4). Allowing diversity support d=n\"'^2/sum_i n_i''^2 for a_rate and exposure count n for a_cov may avoid an unnecessary shared reliability constraint. '\"'\n 'This is a local optimization/representation hypothesis prompted by the observed crossover, not a claim that exposure events or encoded ads are independent samples. '\n 'A mixed assignment must beat the stronger tied assignment AND archived factorized incumbent, then survive independent paired-seed assessment, before claiming added predictive utility. Global novelty is unverified.'),\n 'nearest_work':[\n  {'source_ref':'g2-r0016-diversity_factorized; history_g2_r0016_diversity_factorized.py SHA256 7d113b349957df7b92d51a2f5833f83c8e1bd0eda2b2a0c41b6bbb049f919cf7',\n   'verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Immediate empirical parent and executable starting point. Retain every module and input; activate existing covariance and independently assign its support. The factorized historical result is a mandatory incumbent comparison, not omitted because the new factorial uses joint moments.'},\n  {'source_ref':'g2-r0016-diversity_joint and g2-r0016-exposure_joint; supplied ancestor modules and trial receipts',\n   'verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Closest tied-support alternatives. Reproduce both formulas with two tied endpoint controls; mixed arms change only one component support at a time. No extra trainable parameters or new history fields.'},\n  {'source_ref':'g0-r0003-relation_content_counts; history_g0_r0003_relation_content_counts.py',\n   'verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit target-aware local activation, relation-by-temporal complete-content summaries, explicit relation counts, JointBlock and raw bypasses. This study changes only the later feedback residual supports; it does not introduce those unified representations.'},\n  {'source_ref':'g2-r0004-count_shrink; history_g2_r0004_count_shrink.py',\n   'verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inherit eight old/recent category/brand groups, local fractions and convex interpolation toward the inclusive visible-user rate. The source used one count-conditioned factorized product in a different compressed model; here two moment components receive independent fixed support choices on the stronger relation-content backbone.'},\n  {'source_ref':'paper:din; archived arxiv:1706.06978v4 primary text lines56-97 and307-336',\n   'verification':'read','difference':'Retain adapted target-local activation and Dice; neither is new. The inspected passages establish target-conditioned pooling and adaptive activation, not the proposed component-specific reliability. This is not an exact reproduction of the original training recipe.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet; git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d lines123-170; unirank-benchmark-v2 section2.3 lines31-33',\n   'verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark forward constructs task-mask sequence hubs with per-task projections and layer-wise aggregation/broadcast. Our local study keeps the inherited stack and alters the two scalar support assignments in its residual, without adopting new hubs. Original paper:infnet full text was not available in the authorized cache; no original-method equivalence, external efficacy or priority claim.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:EST; git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0