s use joint moments.'),\n 'predictions':[\n 'Primary directional prediction: rate_div_cov_exp exceeds tied_div, tied_exp and g2-r0016-diversity_factorized on validation macro AUC; reverse assignment is less favorable. This prediction is prospective and may fail.',\n 'Use the complete2x2: rate effect at exposure covariance = rate_div_cov_exp - tied_exp; rate effect at diversity covariance = tied_div - rate_exp_cov_div. Covariance-support effect at diversity rates = rate_div_cov_exp - tied_div; at exposure rates = tied_exp - rate_exp_cov_div. Report all four simple effects and their interaction, even if the candidate loses.',\n 'Tied endpoints should recover the archived joint formulas, initial state and same-seed scores: tied_div against g2-r0016-diversity_joint and tied_exp against g2-r0016-exposure_joint. Matching is an implementation calibration, not an independent replication.',\n 'At shared weights, all-unique ad IDs give d=n and identical residual features for all four arms. Empty slots give zero moments, and empty histories retain zero residual output. With covariance identically zero, changing only covariance support cannot change features; with f=b, the ideal rate-contrast term is zero. Duplicate-heavy slots with nonzero covariance allow component contrasts to differ.',\n 'Expected capacity is32,964,809 total /31,793,216 embedding /1,171,593 dense parameters in every arm, equal to round16; verify on host. Histogram and covariance workloads stay present in every arm. Actual latency, memory and training seconds must be measured, not assumed.',\n 'If authorized host diagnostics expose duplicate-sensitive slices, predeclare history-length bins empty,1-16,17-64,65-100 and concentration bins no identified repetition, d/n in[0,0.5), [0.5,1) per occupied feedback slot. All counts, positive/negative support and aggregation definitions must be recorded; these are exploratory user-level performance diagnostics, not a substitute for full validation. Do not invent currently unavailable slice scores.'\n ],\n 'falsifiers':[\n 'If rate_div_cov_exp fails to exceed either tied joint control or the archived factorized incumbent under the fixed primary selection policy, added predictive utility for the proposed directional implementation is unsupported. Preserve the negative result; a reverse-arm win supports a different direction and requires independent confirmation.',\n 'If tied endpoint initialization/feature/gradient checks fail, or endpoint replay materially differs beyond host-established numerical reproducibility, treat this as an implementation or execution discrepancy before interpreting mixed-arm mechanisms.',\n 'If unique-ID histories or a covariance-zero shared-weight fixture differ across covariance-support-only replacements beyond numerical tolerance, the implementation violates the proposed isolation.',\n 'If gains disappear or reverse in independent paired-seed validation assessment, report one-seed selection noise; deterministic same-seed endpoint matches do not rescue the mechanism claim.',\n 'If capacity differs unexpectedly or measured latency/training cost worsens without sufficient quality benefit, do not claim a capacity-matched or cost-justified improvement. Frozen information/training violations invalidate affected comparisons.'\n ],\n 'alternative_explanations':[\n 'The round16 crossover may reflect one-pass optimization or BF16 trajectory sensitivity rather than statistical reliability; no independent seeds or user-cluster intervals are currently supplied.',\n 'Duplicates can be useful frequency evidence or encoder collisions. Ad concentration need not estimate reliability for category/brand-derived task masks, and low support can regularize useful moments away.',\n 'Overlapping task masks and the inclusive background couple fraction and covariance channels; independent scalar gates do not make the latent mechanisms statistically independent.',\n 'A gain can come from gradient rescaling or feature conditioning 